From: OpenATV STB Kodi Team <oe.patch@openatv.example>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 18:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: allow legacy STB drivers to force GLES2

Some vendor sysroots provide Mesa's GLES3 headers alongside a binary GLES2
implementation.  Detecting the header alone makes Kodi compile and link the
GLES3 capture path even though the driver does not export core GLES3 entry
points such as glBlitFramebuffer.

Add an explicit opt-in for those platforms.  The default auto-detection stays
unchanged, while legacy drivers can select Kodi's existing GLES2 rendering and
capture paths.

---
 cmake/modules/FindOpenGLES.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/modules/FindOpenGLES.cmake b/cmake/modules/FindOpenGLES.cmake
--- a/cmake/modules/FindOpenGLES.cmake
+++ b/cmake/modules/FindOpenGLES.cmake
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ if(NOT TARGET ${APP_NAME_LC}::${CMAKE_FIND_PACKAGE_NAME})
                                               INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES "${OPENGLES_INCLUDE_DIR}"
                                               IMPORTED_NO_SONAME TRUE)
 
-      if(OPENGLES3_INCLUDE_DIR)
+      if(OPENGLES3_INCLUDE_DIR AND NOT OPENGLES_FORCE_GLES2)
         set_property(TARGET ${APP_NAME_LC}::${CMAKE_FIND_PACKAGE_NAME} APPEND PROPERTY
                                                                             INTERFACE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES "${OPENGLES3_INCLUDE_DIR}")
         set_target_properties(${APP_NAME_LC}::${CMAKE_FIND_PACKAGE_NAME} PROPERTIES
